module gunbc.native_compiler_reuse_seed_growth

import gunbc.roadmap_model { RoadmapNodeId }
import gunbc.seed_growth { SeedGrowthJustification }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }

// SEED GROWTH FOR M1.c U2: native-compiler cross-run reuse needs identities it can trust before any
// artifact is served, and this unit makes the existing identities streamed, taken from the observed
// bytes, and carried as values. Operator ruling 2026-09-27 assigned M1.c delivery to this lane and
// admitted U0-U2 to proceed against a pinned base.
//
// MODIFIED, NOT ADDED (ExistingSeedItemModified per gunbc.seed_growth_admission
// SeedGrowthChangeDisposition, not counted as additions, nothing netted against the additions below):
// v1_compiler.cli_run.native_lane_runner sha256_file (streams through sha256_feed_file, same value),
// emitted_closure_identity (streams; an unreadable directory entry refuses instead of silently leaving
// the identity; same value on every successful run), prepare_emitted_compiler_for_entry (the seed
// identity is read first, from the running image; the discriminating red is destructured into the
// preparation), EmittedPreparation (two red fields), SelfHostHeld and
// V2NativeCliHeld (two red fields each), run_self_host and run_v2_native_cli (fill them), and
// v1_compiler.target_invocation_host run_self_host and run_v2_native_cli (the instrument receipt line
// names the red), and v1_compiler.resolved_graph_cache transform_content_digest (reads the running
// image through running_image_path, same value). The .dag authority those identities feed is gunbc.witness_v2_native_route
// NativeRouteReceipt; the instrument lines are gunbc.instrument_targets self_host_label and
// v2_native_cli_label.
data native_compiler_reuse_u2_seed_growth_justification: SeedGrowthJustification = SeedGrowthJustification {
  hand_authored_declarations: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.resolved_graph_cache", decl_name: "running_image_path", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.native_lane_runner.tests", decl_name: "m1c_scratch", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.native_lane_runner.tests", decl_name: "a_streamed_digest_equals_the_one_shot_digest_at_every_buffer_boundary", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.native_lane_runner.tests", decl_name: "the_closure_identity_is_name_then_bytes_over_sorted_rs_files", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.native_lane_runner.tests", decl_name: "a_file_larger_than_the_memory_cap_digests_under_the_cap", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.native_lane_runner.tests", decl_name: "the_seed_identity_is_the_running_image_after_the_path_is_replaced", field: WholeDeclaration }
  ],

  reason: "The native route's identities are about to become the inputs of a cross-run key (M1.c NativeCompilerArtifactRequest), and three of them could not carry that weight. The executable and seed digests read whole files into memory, so the memory an identity costs grew with the artifact; sha256_feed_file streams through a fixed 64 KiB buffer and gives the same SHA-256 value. The seed identity re-opened a file NAME minutes after emission, so a seed rebuilt in the meantime was refused as unreadable or, if the rename landed between lookup and open, recorded a binary that did not emit the closure; it is now read before the emission from the running image, through running_image_path -- the one selection of that path, factored out of resolved_graph_cache transform_content_digest rather than written a second time (/proc/self/exe on Linux, the start path elsewhere, so a non-Linux host keeps the behavior it had). The discriminating red was checked, printed and dropped, so a build later served from a store could not be admitted on the red it established; it is now the preparation's value and the instruments print it. WHY RUST: every item is a host effect on the route's own files and process image (open/read, the running image) inside the seed's native lane runner, which runs no interpreter; there is no .dag route to these bytes. PURPOSE ADMISSION under gunbc.v1_maintenance_standing v1_seed_standing (SemanticsFrozen, MaintenanceActive): it serves the v2 self-host program's native route. Streaming is a bounded operational fix with an unchanged value; the running-image seed identity is a defect repair; carrying the red preserves behavior. None of it is PublicSurfaceGrowth (no verb, flag or public item; the instrument receipt line only names what the instrument already established), none is NewEscapeHatchOrAdmissionRow (nothing is admitted that refused before), and none is SeedFeatureCompletion (no new capability the successor lacks). CONSUMERS (DESIGN section 3c): the streamed identities and the red are consumed by execution now -- the route and both instruments read them. (A probe-root footprint measurement was withdrawn from this unit: no executing consumer reads it -- the store's capacity admission reads the stored part's own size -- so it was a one-off measurement, taken once and recorded in the PR, not an instrument.) The controls are local receipts because no CI step runs this crate's unit tests (gunbc.rung_drop rust_unit_tests_off_the_merge_path).",

  owning_dissolution_lane: "v1-hand-queue-drain" as RoadmapNodeId,

  trigger: "Delete these items when the native route's preparation -- emission, crate assembly, build, identity and the discriminating red -- is performed by a native v2 generation rather than by the seed's native lane runner, so that the seed is no longer the producer whose identities a cross-run key reads. WHAT DOES NOT RETIRE THEM: moving the digest into another seed file; replacing SHA-256 with another family in the same function; or M1.c serving from a store while the seed still prepares every miss. Each leaves the seed as the producer of the identities.",

  current_boundary: "src/v1/stage0/src/resolved_graph_cache.rs running_image_path and the native_lane_runner tests above (the streamed digest this unit introduced moved to v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host sha256_feed_file with U1a, and is cited by that row), called from prepare_emitted_compiler_for_entry behind gunbc test //v2/test/..., //gunbc/instruments:self-host and //gunbc/instruments:v2-native-cli"
}

// M1.c U1a: THE PROBE BUILD RUNS A CONCRETE, IDENTIFIED TOOLCHAIN UNDER A CONSTRUCTED ENVIRONMENT.
//
// MODIFIED, NOT ADDED (ExistingSeedItemModified, nothing netted): v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host
// ProbeCargoInvocation (cargo path and identity, environment names and digest, configuration),
// probe_cargo_command_bound (runs the toolchain's own cargo, clears and rebuilds the environment,
// binds RUSTC to the toolchain's own rustc), probe_cargo_command (constructs, resolves, observes),
// resolve_probe_compiler (now the ENTRY compiler the toolchain is selected from), and
// v1_compiler.cli_run.native_lane_runner sha256_file, emitted_closure_identity and
// prepare_emitted_compiler_for_entry (read the moved digest; print the build inputs). DELETED:
// v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host probe_compiler_identity (replaced by probe_tool_identity,
// which runs under the build's own environment) and v1_compiler.cli_run.native_lane_runner
// sha256_feed_file (moved here, one home for the streamed identity). The .dag authority for the
// admitted names is v2.extdeps.languages.rust rust_host_build_environment.
data native_compiler_reuse_u1a_seed_growth_justification: SeedGrowthJustification = SeedGrowthJustification {
  hand_authored_declarations: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host", decl_name: "RUST_HOST_BUILD_ENVIRONMENT_NAMES", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host", decl_name: "ProbeEnvironment", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host", decl_name: "probe_environment_from", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host", decl_name: "constructed_probe_environment", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host", decl_name: "sha256_feed_file", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host", decl_name: "sha256_file_streamed", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host", decl_name: "probe_tool_identity", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host", decl_name: "ProbeToolchain", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host", decl_name: "resolve_probe_toolchain", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host", decl_name: "cargo_configuration_observation", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host.tests", decl_name: "fixture_toolchain", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host.tests", decl_name: "u1a_scratch", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host.tests", decl_name: "the_constructed_environment_admits_the_row_by_exact_name_and_nothing_else", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host.tests", decl_name: "the_spawn_runs_the_toolchains_cargo_even_when_cargo_is_planted", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host.tests", decl_name: "cargo_configuration_is_observed_and_an_unreadable_one_refuses", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host.tests", decl_name: "a_sysroot_without_cargo_refuses_rather_than_falling_back", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host.tests", decl_name: "planted_build_variables_cannot_change_the_probe_build_bytes", field: WholeDeclaration }
  ],

  reason: "M1.c keys a stored compiler on the inputs that produce its bytes, so every input the build can see must either be in the key or be unable to reach the build. The probe build inherited this process's whole environment and ran whatever `$CARGO` or `cargo` on PATH resolved at spawn time, next to a RUSTC that was usually a rustup proxy: an ambient CARGO_PROFILE_*, CARGO_INCREMENTAL, RUSTC_BOOTSTRAP or CC could change the executable under an unchanged key, and the receipt named a proxy rather than the compiler that ran. Now the environment is cleared and rebuilt from the admitted names of v2.extdeps.languages.rust rust_host_build_environment, with a digest; the entry compiler is asked which sysroot it selects and the build runs that sysroot's own cargo and binds RUSTC to its own rustc, both identified under the build's environment from the crate's directory; and every cargo configuration file discovery would read is recorded with its digest. The facts are printed until U7 carries them in the receipt, and U3 reads them into the key. WHY RUST: the subject is the seed's own cargo spawn in the emit-compile host, which runs no interpreter. PURPOSE ADMISSION under gunbc.v1_maintenance_standing v1_seed_standing: it serves the v2 self-host program's native route; it is a bounded operational fix that adds refusals (ProbeToolchainUnresolved, CargoConfigurationUnreadable) and admits nothing that refused before -- not NewEscapeHatchOrAdmissionRow, not PublicSurfaceGrowth (no verb, flag or public item), not SeedFeatureCompletion. A STATED DIVERGENCE, NOT A SILENT FORK: v1_compiler.v1_interpreter emit_host_constructed_build_environment, emit_host_cargo_configuration_digest and observe_tool_identity answer the same questions for the emit-host transport with a 64-bit non-cryptographic hash and whole-file reads; this host needs SHA-256 over streamed bytes for a cross-run key. TRIGGER FOR UNIFYING THEM: extdeps.realization.emit_on_demand_host ResolvedBuildContext moving to a std.content_hash cryptographic family, after which both hosts read one construction. The admitted-name list is a seed copy of the .dag row; its executing drift control is the U7 admission clause that compares the recorded names to the row inside the emitted binary, and until then it is review diligence.",

  owning_dissolution_lane: "v1-hand-queue-drain" as RoadmapNodeId,

  trigger: "Delete these items when the probe build is a modeled transport that reads its admitted environment, toolchain selection and configuration observation from extdeps.realization.emit_on_demand_host ResolvedBuildContext and v2.std.host_transport HostBuildEnvironment, performed by a native v2 generation rather than the seed's emit-compile host. WHAT DOES NOT RETIRE THEM: moving the list into another seed file, widening the admitted names by prefix, or recording the environment without clearing it.",

  current_boundary: "src/v1/stage0/src/emitted_closure_compile_host.rs probe_cargo_command -> constructed_probe_environment, resolve_probe_toolchain, cargo_configuration_observation, probe_cargo_command_bound; reached by every probe build: the required emit-compile phase, //gunbc/instruments:self-host, :v2-native-cli, :emitted-crate-workspace and gunbc test //v2/test/..."
}

// M1.c U1c: A BUILD'S DIRECTORIES DO NOT REACH ITS BYTES.
//
// MODIFIED, NOT ADDED (ExistingSeedItemModified, nothing netted): v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host
// probe_cargo_command_bound (sets the composed flags on both channels and records them) and
// probe_cargo_command (composes them from the run's directories). The .dag authority is
// gunbc.emitted_build_reproducibility emitted_build_rustflags, which the route's admission reconstructs
// (gunbc.witness_v2_native_route native_route_emitted_build_paths_remapped).
data native_compiler_reuse_u1c_seed_growth_justification: SeedGrowthJustification = SeedGrowthJustification {
  hand_authored_declarations: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host", decl_name: "REMAP_PATH_PREFIX_FLAG", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host", decl_name: "REMAPPED_CRATE_DIR", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host", decl_name: "REMAPPED_TARGET_DIR", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host", decl_name: "REMAPPED_CARGO_HOME", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host", decl_name: "ProbeBuildFlags", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host", decl_name: "probe_build_flags", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host", decl_name: "probe_cargo_home", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host.tests", decl_name: "the_probe_build_flags_are_the_declared_composition", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host.tests", decl_name: "a_directory_the_remap_cannot_spell_refuses", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host.tests", decl_name: "the_cargo_home_is_the_declared_one_or_cargos_default_or_a_refusal", field: WholeDeclaration }
  ],

  reason: "Measured (M1.c U0, 2026-09-28): the emitted v2.compiler.compile crate built in two directories gave two different executables, because rustc wrote absolute source paths into the binary; with the crate directory, the target directory and the cargo home remapped, the two were byte-identical, and one path built twice was identical too. A cross-run key cannot name a directory that differs on every run (and CI's cargo home is fresh per job), so each probe build now sets the warning denial followed by three remaps to fixed spellings, on both RUSTFLAGS channels, and records the composed flags. Cargo's own trim-paths profile setting would do this without flags but is not stable on the pinned toolchain (cargo 1.93.0 refuses it). The spellings mirror gunbc.emitted_build_reproducibility, whose composition the route's admission reconstructs from the recorded flags and refuses on any difference (emitted_build_paths_not_remapped), so a drift between this copy and the row reds the route. A directory the form cannot spell (relative, whitespace, `=`) refuses before the build (ProbePathNotRemappable), as does a build with no cargo home (ProbeCargoHomeUnresolved). WHY RUST: the subject is the seed's cargo spawn in the emit-compile host, which runs no interpreter. PURPOSE ADMISSION under gunbc.v1_maintenance_standing v1_seed_standing: it serves the v2 self-host program's native route; a bounded operational fix whose only admission-side change adds a refusal; not PublicSurfaceGrowth, not NewEscapeHatchOrAdmissionRow, not SeedFeatureCompletion.",

  owning_dissolution_lane: "v1-hand-queue-drain" as RoadmapNodeId,

  trigger: "Delete these items when the probe build is a modeled transport that reads its flags from gunbc.emitted_build_reproducibility rather than a seed copy, performed by a native v2 generation; OR when the pinned toolchain's cargo stabilizes profile trim-paths and the probe manifest carries it instead of flags, at which point the admission clause is restated over the manifest. WHAT DOES NOT RETIRE THEM: pinning every build to one fixed directory (it serializes concurrent runs and still leaks the cargo home), or remapping only the crate directory.",

  current_boundary: "src/v1/stage0/src/emitted_closure_compile_host.rs probe_cargo_command -> probe_build_flags(crate_dir, target_dir, probe_cargo_home) -> probe_cargo_command_bound; reached by every probe build: the required emit-compile phase, //gunbc/instruments:self-host, :v2-native-cli, :emitted-crate-workspace and gunbc test //v2/test/..."
}

